# NOTE: .gitignore has no inline comments. A "#" only starts a comment at the
# START of a line — anywhere else it is part of the pattern, which silently
# does nothing and leaves the file tracked. Keep every comment on its own line.

# --- What Wawi records about YOU ---------------------------------------
# This is the section that matters most. Wawi listens to a room and looks at
# a screen; everything below is a recording of that. None of it is source
# code, and committing any of it publishes what was said and seen near the
# machine — to anyone who can read the repository, and it stays in history
# even after a later deletion.

# Verbatim transcript of every exchange.
conversation.log
# Standing instructions, in the user's own words.
preferences.txt
# Auto-filed problems; their context quotes what you said.
issues/
# Screen captures taken when no project was named.
screenshots/
# Screen captures dropped into a worktree for an agent to open.
.wawi-shots/
**/.wawi-shots/

# --- Runtime output -------------------------------------------------------
# Covers answers.log too, which is the readable transcript the background
# launcher writes: same content as conversation.log, same reason to keep it out.
*.log
# Written by scripts/wawictl while it runs in the background (jarvis.pid is
# the name it had before the rename).
wawi.pid
jarvis.pid

# --- Local audio artefacts ------------------------------------------------
# Spike and diagnostic scripts write these next to the source.
*.wav

# --- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# --- Virtualenvs ----------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- Editors and OS -------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# --- Local tooling state --------------------------------------------------
.atl/
.claude/
.mcp.json

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*

# --- Stray images in the project root ----------------------------------------
# Mascot art lives under wawi/assets/; a loose image at the root is a local
# scratch file (or a screenshot) that should never be published by accident.
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.png

# --- Local configuration --------------------------------------------------
# config.yaml is YOUR machine: min_speech_level is your room's noise floor,
# silence_ms is how long you pause when you think, phrases is what you chose
# to call it. config.yaml.example is the tracked template to copy.
config.yaml

# --- HUD geometry (set by dragging, not by editing) -----------------------
panel_state.json

# Durable rolling memory (wawi/recall.py) — a transcript of the room,
# same reason to keep it out as conversation.log.
recall.txt

# Interrupted turn or task (wawi/inflight.py) — it quotes what you asked for.
inflight.json
inflight.json.tmp

# Generated TTS clips used by the noise tests (not a real voice)
!tests/fixtures/*.wav
